{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  "How it's made" and "Pour it with", rebuilt against the design.

  The design runs the numbered steps down the left in a 44px/1fr grid with the
  ingredient list ruled off beneath them, and a full-bleed process photograph
  filling the right half. The port had the steps but neither the number column
  nor the image.

  Steps come from custom.process_steps (JSON) if present, otherwise from
  custom.process, which the live store holds as prose in "HEADING - body"
  blocks separated by blank lines.

  The process image falls back through: custom.process_image, then the
  product's second media item, then its featured image — so the panel is never
  empty on a product with photography.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign steps = product.metafields.custom.process_steps.value
  assign prose = product.metafields.custom.process | metafield_text | strip
  assign pairings = product.metafields.custom.pairings.value
  assign ingredients = product.metafields.custom.ingredients | metafield_text

  # The section setting wins, so this panel's image can be changed in the
  # editor per template without touching product data. Below it the original
  # chain still applies, which is what keeps all 27 products populated without
  # anyone opening the editor.
  #
  # These are hash comments. A comment TAG here is a syntax error: inside a
  # liquid block the enclosing tag ends at the first closing delimiter it meets,
  # so a nested tag cuts the block short and everything after becomes stray
  # markup. Shopify then rejects the file and silently keeps serving the
  # previous version — which is exactly what happened. This section sat frozen
  # on the staging theme from 31 July through two later commits that both
  # pushed cleanly. check.py rule 1b now catches it.
  #
  # Note there are deliberately no brace-percent sequences in this comment:
  # a closing delimiter inside the prose would end the block just as surely.
  assign process_image = section.settings.image
  if process_image == blank
    assign process_image = product.metafields.custom.process_image.value
  endif
  if process_image == blank
    assign process_image = product.media[1]
  endif
  if process_image == blank
    assign process_image = product.featured_media
  endif

  assign media_ratio = section.settings.media_ratio | default: 'portrait'
-%}

{%- if steps != blank or prose != blank -%}
  <div class="non-process">
    <div class="non-process__copy">
      <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.steps_heading }}</div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Three sources, in priority order: Step blocks, then the process_steps
        JSON metafield, then the prose metafield split on blank lines.

        Blocks come first so the section is editable at all — it had no block
        types, so the theme editor offered two headings and nothing else while
        the five visible steps came from per-product data with no way to touch
        them from here.

        Blocks are an OVERRIDE, not a replacement. Step copy is genuinely
        per-product — NON1's raspberries are not NON5's hibiscus — so the
        metafield stays the default and blocks win only where someone has
        deliberately added them. Adding a Step block to the default product
        template would otherwise give all nine bottles the same process.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign step_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'step' -%}

      <div class="non-steps">
        {%- if step_blocks.size > 0 -%}
          {%- for block in step_blocks -%}
            <div class="non-step" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="non-step__n">
                {{- block.settings.number | default: forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -}}
              </div>
              <div>
                <div class="non-step__t">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
                <p class="non-step__b">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}

        {%- elsif steps != blank -%}
          {%- for step in steps -%}
            <div class="non-step">
              <div class="non-step__n">{{ step.n }}</div>
              <div>
                <div class="non-step__t">{{ step.title }}</div>
                <p class="non-step__b">{{ step.body }}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}

        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Split on the SECTION KEYWORDS, not on blank lines.

            Checked every bottle against the live store: NON1 is the only one
            whose custom.process separates sections with a blank line. NON2,
            NON3, NON5 and NON7 use a single newline. Splitting on a blank line
            therefore gave NON1 five steps and every other bottle exactly one —
            the whole process crushed into step 01 "Fruit" with "TANNIN -",
            "SALINITY -" and the rest buried mid-paragraph. That is what made
            the other PDPs look nothing like NON1: the theme was correct only
            for the one product whose data happened to match the parser.

            Keying on the keywords makes the parse independent of how the prose
            is typed, so a merchandiser reformatting a metafield cannot silently
            collapse a product's process again. A product using none of the
            keywords falls back to the old blank-line split.

            &nbsp; is stripped because NON3 and NON5 hold it literally — it was
            rendering as the visible characters "&nbsp;" mid-sentence.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign norm = prose | replace: '&nbsp;', ' '
            assign norm = norm | replace: '&amp;nbsp;', ' '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'FRUIT - ', '~~FRUIT - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'TANNIN - ', '~~TANNIN - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'SALINITY - ', '~~SALINITY - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'ACIDITY - ', '~~ACIDITY - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'BALANCE - ', '~~BALANCE - '
          -%}
          {%- if norm contains '~~' -%}
            {%- assign chunks = norm | split: '~~' -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign chunks = norm | split: '

' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- for chunk in chunks -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign clean = chunk | strip
              assign bits = clean | split: ' - '
              assign title = bits | first | strip
              assign body = clean | remove_first: title | remove_first: ' - ' | strip
              assign n = forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2
            -%}
            {%- if clean != blank -%}
              <div class="non-step">
                <div class="non-step__n">{{ n }}</div>
                <div>
                  {%- if body != blank and title.size < 40 -%}
                    <div class="non-step__t">{{ title | capitalize }}</div>
                    <p class="non-step__b">{{ body }}</p>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <p class="non-step__b">{{ clean }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if ingredients != blank -%}
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--non-line);padding-top:18px">
          <div class="non-spec__k">{{ section.settings.ingredients_label }}</div>
          <div class="non-step__b" style="margin-top:8px;max-width:46ch">{{ ingredients }}</div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="non-process__media non-process__media--{{ media_ratio }}">
      {%- if process_image != blank -%}
        {{
          process_image
          | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp'
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            widths: '600,900,1200',
            class: 'non-process__img',
            alt: product.title
        }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Pairing cards, same override rule as the steps: Pairing blocks win, the
  metafield is the default. Pairings are per-product too — the engine derives
  them — so blocks are for overriding one bottle, not for authoring all nine.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pair_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'pairing' -%}
{%- if pair_blocks.size > 0 or pairings != blank -%}
  <div class="non-section" style="border-top:1px solid var(--non-line)">
    <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.pairings_heading }}</div>

    <div class="non-pairs">
      {%- if pair_blocks.size > 0 -%}
        {%- for block in pair_blocks -%}
          <div class="non-pair-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="non-pair-card__t">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
            <p class="non-pair-card__b">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- for pair in pairings -%}
          <div class="non-pair-card">
            <div class="non-pair-card__t">{{ pair.title }}</div>
            <p class="non-pair-card__b">{{ pair.body }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Process & pairings",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "steps_heading",
      "label": "Process heading",
      "default": "How it's made — not de-alcoholised"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pairings_heading",
      "label": "Pairings heading",
      "default": "Pour it with"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Media"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Process image",
      "info": "Overrides the product's process image. Left empty, it falls back to the product's own process metafield, then its second media item, then its featured image."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_ratio",
      "label": "Image shape",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "square",
          "label": "Square (1:1)"
        },
        {
          "value": "tall",
          "label": "Tall (4:5)"
        },
        {
          "value": "portrait",
          "label": "Portrait (3:4)"
        },
        {
          "value": "fill",
          "label": "Fill the panel"
        }
      ],
      "default": "portrait"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ingredients_label",
      "label": "Ingredients label",
      "default": "Ingredients"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Process & pairings"
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Overrides the product's process_steps metafield for THIS template only. Leave the section with no Step blocks to keep using each product's own data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "Fruit"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Body"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "number",
          "label": "Number",
          "info": "Optional. Auto-numbers from position when empty."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pairing",
      "name": "Pairing card",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Overrides the product's pairings metafield for THIS template only."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Body"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
